# === Test fixture binary rule (project convention, added v0.66.0) ===
# Binary test fixtures (videos, images, 3D models, archives, audio, HDR
# textures) live under the tests/ subtree and are NEVER committed to git.
# They are auto-ignored by extension so a stray fixture can never
# accidentally pollute history.
# Test CODE (tests/*.test.js) is ALWAYS committed -- the project relies on
# `npm test` against this convention. To force-commit a binary fixture
# (rare; e.g., a versioned reference model), use `git add -f <path>` and
# document WHY in the commit message.
#
# SCOPE IS NARROW BY DESIGN: patterns below only auto-ignore binaries under
# tests/**. A .mp4 / .glb / .wav / .hdr placed in any other location
# (src/, public/, repo root) WILL be tracked unless explicitly gitignored.
# When introducing a new asset folder outside tests/, add its exclusion
# to .gitignore at the same time the folder is created -- do not rely on
# this rule alone. See AGENTS.md "Conventions -> Test-fixture binary rule"
# for the full project rule.
tests/**/*.mp4
tests/**/*.mov
tests/**/*.webm
tests/**/*.avi
tests/**/*.mkv
tests/**/*.mpg
tests/**/*.mpeg
tests/**/*.wmv
tests/**/*.flv
tests/**/*.m4v
tests/**/*.png
tests/**/*.jpg
tests/**/*.jpeg
tests/**/*.gif
tests/**/*.bmp
tests/**/*.tiff
tests/**/*.webp
tests/**/*.glb
tests/**/*.gltf
tests/**/*.fbx
tests/**/*.obj
tests/**/*.blend
tests/**/*.dae
tests/**/*.zip
tests/**/*.tar
tests/**/*.tar.gz
tests/**/*.tgz
tests/**/*.7z
tests/**/*.rar
# Audio (Web Audio API in tech-stack; test fixtures for future audio layer)
tests/**/*.wav
tests/**/*.mp3
tests/**/*.flac
tests/**/*.ogg
tests/**/*.aac
tests/**/*.m4a
# Modern image + Apple 3D (future-proof)
tests/**/*.heic
tests/**/*.avif
tests/**/*.usdz
# HDR textures (project ships nebula skydome; IBL test fixtures are a
# plausible near-future need)
tests/**/*.hdr
tests/**/*.exr

# === One-off downloads convention (fixes the v0.66.0 git-bloat issue) ===
# Recursive download folders for transient / one-off content. The scripts
# that WRITE INTO these folders ARE committed (e.g. mark13/download_video.py);
# the downloaded data itself is NEVER committed.
mark13/downloads/
